WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.610
<v A>Before a card goes anywhere, someone has to be allowed to build it. That is governance, and every client has four corners of it.

2
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.210
<v B>Four corners. Where do we start?

3
00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.530
<v A>Who may build AI tools?

4
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:23.670
<v A>In some companies anyone can build an assistant over a weekend. In others only IT may. Your card has to fit that rule.

5
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.450
<v B>And the second corner?

6
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.560
<v A>Which tools are approved?

7
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:40.150
<v A>If the tool on your card is not on the approved list, add the approval time to your plan. At NorthRiver, Lin's AI policy is still in legal review, so nothing is approved yet.

8
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.020
<v B>So the tool question waits on legal.

9
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.190
<v A>Who collects the requests?

10
00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:54.880
<v A>When every department sends its own AI requests, the same idea gets built three times. One place should collect them, and your cards go there.

11
00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.530
<v B>And the last corner?

12
00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.240
<v A>Who signs off?

13
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:07.300
<v A>Name who approves a card before it ships: security, legal, the sponsor. If nobody can, that is a finding too.

14
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.480
<v B>Is that the whole of governance?

15
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:18.540
<v A>No. Modules 3 and 6 go deeper. For now, check the four corners for every card, and write down what you do not know.
